26.11.177	The screen no longer flashes white when it turns back on, or between the two birds as the OpenFrame starts.
26.11.176	A touch now always turns the screen back on, where it could sometimes stay dark.
26.11.175	The screen no longer turns itself back on now and then while it's meant to be off.
26.11.170	The OpenFrame Flash screen no longer comes up garbled, with lines doubled and out of place.
26.11.162	The settings folder on the OpenFrame's boot volume has a README.txt saying what each file is for.
26.11.161	If an update's new kernel won't start, the OpenFrame goes back to the one before by itself.
26.11.157	The bird stays on the screen while the OpenFrame starts, with a bar under it, instead of a black screen and a blinking cursor.
26.11.151	Settings, Audio has a new "Mix at 48 kHz" switch, for an OpenFrame mostly used for video.
26.11.150	Sound at another rate than your OpenFrame's (48 kHz video, say) is now resampled cleanly, without the false high tones it had.
26.11.149	Direct to DAC is now remembered for each DAC separately, so a second DAC no longer starts at full volume.
26.11.142	Change the sound output and what's playing follows it.
26.11.137	Play through a USB DAC: plug it in, and the sound goes there.
26.11.134	Give the OpenFrame a name, in Settings under About.
26.11.130	Choose when the OpenFrame updates itself, in Settings under Updates.
26.11.121	The OpenFrame now keeps itself up to date overnight, and restarts at about 4am when an update needs it.
26.11.117	The SSH server stays off until there's a way to log in, by password or key.
